WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.553
(audience clapping)
- Good evening, everyone.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:08.070
It is really my distinct
pleasure and privilege

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.020
to be with all of you tonight,

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.670
here, as we celebrate

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:16.000
the Academy's 14th
Annual Governor's Awards.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
(audience clapping)

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.900
We are looking forward to
a beautiful night ahead,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.370
as we come together

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.330
after a year challenged
by unprecedented heartache

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.620
and struggle for many,

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.300
both within our industry

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.853
and also around the world.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.460
We know though that light

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.770
can always find its way into darkness,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:44.190
and tonight, we hope
to bring you some light

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.040
by celebrating four icons of our industry

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.230
who have each brightened our lives

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.380
through their immeasurable
contributions of joy,

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.930
transcendent moments of beauty

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.800
and numerous pathways for finding awe.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.480
Thank you all for sitting down

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.430
and being quiet in the back.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.543
Appreciate it.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.630
This is in fact what we,
as film artists, can do,

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.030
inspire awe.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.480
A professor who studied the
transformative power of awe

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.790
says it can be derived from many sources,

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.890
of course, nature, music,

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.630
art, religion.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.260
But the one that I find most
resonant to our community

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.580
is through what he calls
collective effervescence.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.830
In each corner of the world,

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.950
countless individuals
sitting in a movie theater

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.650
have experienced that ineffable gift

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.080
of collective effervescence.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.683
And perhaps, tonight, we
shall have a taste of it, too.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.550
Each of our honorees has
contributed to that gift

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.800
in one way or another.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.370
With Angela Bassett, it has
been through her magnetic

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:58.370
and mesmerizing performances.
(audience clapping)

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.890
With Mel Brooks, through his prolific work

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.450
as both a master comedian

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.143
and producer. (clapping)
(audience clapping)

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.260
With Carol Littleton,

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.720
through her magical touch in storytelling

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.100
and many years of service

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.550
to the academy.
(audience cheering)

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:21.783
What a beautiful room.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.670
And with Michelle Satter.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:26.790
(audience cheering)
Through expanding and drawing

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:30.663
brilliant new horizons
for so many artists.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.080
Many of you this evening
are members of our Academy,

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.710
you understand the innate
value of close collaboration

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.320
and community building in our work.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.780
You have shared with us how
important it is, therefore,

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.790
to come together in person,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.620
whether it be for screenings,

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.770
or to discuss the pressing
issues of our industry,

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.740
or by attending celebratory
events like this one,

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:00.000
where we express particular
admiration and gratitude

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.020
for the contributions of
four amazing individuals

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:08.610
carefully chosen by our
esteemed Board of Governors.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.260
I could not be more honored

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.940
to help lead this organization

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.500
along with Academy CEO,

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.343
Bill Kramer. (clapping)
(audience cheering)

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.310
And we are so fortunate to be supported

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.510
by the stellar work

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:27.960
done by so many of our members and staff,

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.550
not just tonight,

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.920
not just during Oscar season,

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.020
but day in and day out,

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:39.020
365 days a year. (clapping)
(audience clapping)

00:03:42.178 --> 00:03:44.820
I'd also like to take
a moment to thank Rolex

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.089
for its generous support.

00:03:46.089 --> 00:03:48.148
(audience clapping)
Both this evening

00:03:48.148 --> 00:03:51.990
and of the Academy and
our museum year round.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.810
Rolex's commitment to the arts
and sciences of filmmaking

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:58.113
is paramount to furthering
our important work.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.812
Thank you also to the
wonderful Jennifer Fox.

00:04:01.812 --> 00:04:02.880
(audience clapping)
For, again, producing

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.500
such a beautiful night for us.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.010
We're deeply grateful for
her creativity and support.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.710
And special thanks to our
brilliant Academy staff

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:14.730
and production teams

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.800
for their incredible work.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.800
Also, thanks to our four ASL interpreters

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.510
for supporting us to make this evening

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.921
accessible to all. (clapping)
(audience clapping)

00:04:22.921 --> 00:04:25.921
(audience cheering)

00:04:27.301 --> 00:04:29.340
And please also welcome alumni

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.497
from our GOLD mentorship program

00:04:31.497 --> 00:04:34.523
who are acting as our trophy presenters.

00:04:34.523 --> 00:04:36.990
(audience member laughing)
(audience clapping)

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:41.100
Thank you all so much for joining us.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.520
I would like to toast
each and every one of you,

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.726
and wish you a most extraordinary evening.

00:04:47.726 --> 00:04:50.309
(upbeat music)

